    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba267b14_546530d9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 190,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T14:58:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Extra review :)\n\nSo this call returns a VkResult object and we\u0027re suppose to check to see if it returns VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED or not (well if you follow the general pattern in Vulkan). Now technically, what we\u0027re doing here is safe because this one function is weird and early specs didn\u0027t have the return value and said that all property values will be filled to 0 if unsupported. This is left in the current specs for backwards compatibility. But we should probably do things the intended way and check the return value. See https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/1.1-extensions/html/vkspec.html#capabilities-image",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 190,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "a15d58e25db5c52cac51f8904f967d4244c7558b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b345ca00_7d3a6470",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 190,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-11T20:36:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good context to have! Alright, so it looks like GetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties can return 3 possible failure modes (VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY). So I made it such that any result that is not VK_SUCCESS logs a warning and returns. Let me know if this is agreeable. We could do more in-depth failure mode messages depending upon the code returned if you think that would be worthwhile.",
      "parentUuid": "ba267b14_546530d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
